<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU urges public bodies, markets to get ready for E.</title>
<headline>EU urges public bodies, markets to get ready for E.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The EU will urge public authorities and the financial sector to intensify their preparations for the launch of economic and monetary union (EMU), a draft communique shows.</p>
<p>The draft, due to be endorsed and formally released later on Saturday, said, &quot;The European Council welcomes the further decisive progress which has been made in the preparations for EMU...</p>
<p>&quot;The European Council therefore urges the institutions, public authorities and economic agents to intensify their preparations for the starting date of 1 January 1999.&quot;</p>
</text>
